   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The final modeling data is numeric and model-ready. Categorical variables were one-hot encoded during the preprocessing pipeline.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Modeling Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a binary classification problem. The modeling strategy compares an interpretable baseline model (logistic regression) with more flexible classifier models.\n",
    "\n",
    "The models used are:\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  Logistic Regression\n",
    "2.  Random Forest Classifier\n",
    "3.  Histogram Gradient Boosting Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "Logistic regression is used as the baseline because it is interpretable and produces probabilities naturally. Random Forest and Histogram Gradient Boosting are included because they can capture nonlinear relationships and interactions among borrower, loan, and property characteristics. `mi_cancel` was dropped post script due to an error."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "8a567ceb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x_train= x_train.drop(columns=[\"mi_cancel\"], errors=\"ignore\")\n",
    "x_test= x_test.drop(columns=[\"mi_cancel\"], errors=\"ignore\")"
   ]
  },
